+    // Creates the underlying OS thread of every AutomaticThread registered on this condition,
+    // without giving any of them work. A thread started this way polls once, finds nothing, and
+    // parks on the condition until either work arrives or the idle timeout elapses.
+    //
+    // This exists for embedders that install a syscall filter denying thread creation: after the
+    // filter is installed an AutomaticThread can never be created, so the complete set has to be
+    // brought up while creation is still permitted. The alternative — handing a worklist token
+    // work purely so its thread is born as a side effect — depends on that work still reaching the
+    // queue, and silently stops creating the thread the day the work is short-circuited.
+    //
+    // Pin the idle timeout before calling this, or a thread may retire in the window between this
+    // call and the filter, and retirement is unrecoverable once creation is denied.
+    //
+    // Returns how many threads were started. A caller whose threads keep a running count of who is
+    // awake has to add this in: a thread started here polls once and parks, and parking decrements
+    // that count whether or not anything ever incremented it.
+    WTF_EXPORT_PRIVATE unsigned startAllThreads(const AbstractLocker&);
